    "title": "Singular and Plural Nouns Adding -s and -es",
    "channel": "Mrs. Montgomery's Learning Corner"
  },
  "steps": [
    "Singular means ONE: one dog, one mango, one box.",
    "Plural means MORE THAN ONE. Most nouns just add -s: dog → dogs.",
    "If a noun ends in s, x, ch, or sh, add -es: box → boxes, beach → beaches.",
    "Some nouns are tricky and change completely: child → children, foot → feet, mouse → mice!"
  ],
